  "id": "muscle-spindle",
  "term": "muscle spindle",
  "definition": "A muscle spindle is a sensory structure in skeletal muscle made of intrafusal fibers that run alongside the main muscle fibers. When the muscle is stretched, it signals the spinal cord and helps trigger a reflex contraction that opposes further stretch, supporting normal muscle tone and indicating muscle length rather than muscle tension.",
